import json
def add_quadratic(d,P,new_page,para,table):
 O=P/'engineering-v19-results/quadratic-contact'
 if not (O/'verification.json').exists():return
 s=json.loads((O/'status.json').read_text());v=json.loads((O/'verification.json').read_text());c=json.loads((P/'engineering-v19-results/conforming-contact/status.json').read_text());new_page(d,'V19 Higher order joint model')
 para(d,'The first linear solid joint model still changed by about 6 percent at the finest mesh comparison. A separate model variant aligns the washer boundary and preload footprint with the mesh, then uses quadratic solid elements. Its contact faces are split into small linear triangles. This improves the bulk bending approximation; it is still the same ideal pivot and prescribed preload concept, not a real bolt or complete worn headset.')
 para(d,'We kept the earlier '+str(len(c['cases']))+' washer boundary pilot cases and all 22 original joint cases. The pilot made little difference to the linear solid result. The new quadratic variant has '+str(len(s['cases']))+' nominal outward fixture cases, comparing 3 mm and 2.3 mm settings for child large and adult small. The later inward extension is recorded in the next chapter. Other friction settings were not repeated with quadratic solids, so these results do not replace every earlier load case.')
 para(d,'The first adult mesh had a curved cell that folded inside out, so we rejected it. The retry adjusts the high order mesh and retains the failed log. Accepted meshes must keep positive local cell volumes, checked through their Jacobians. The reference fixture uses 140 N preload, assumed friction 0.2 and 2 N outward load. This is not a measured setting for the proposed 160 Nmm hinge target.')
 table(d,['Family','Mesh displacement change','Chosen 5 percent comparison'],[[r['size'].replace('_',' '),f"{r['change_percent']:.2f}%",'Pass' if r['gate'] else 'Fail'] for r in s['cases'] if r['change_percent'] is not None],[2.7,2.0,2.2])
 para(d,'The element controls reproduce a constant strain and its analytic strain energy on a straight tetrahedron. The volume and matrix symmetry controls also pass. Each element uses 27 positive integration points. Saved displacement, contact force, friction, force balance and source hashes were rechecked for '+str(len(v['array_audits']))+' solves. The mesh volumes differ from the reference CAD component volumes by less than the chosen 1 percent check.')
 para(d,'A passing displacement comparison applies only to this selected outward fixture, these two meshes and the assumed material and contact laws. It does not prove convergence for every stress, load, friction value or hardware part. Stress is sampled at element centres. Actual friction, bolt and bearing behaviour, material conditioning, creep and a full worn model remain unvalidated. The earlier failed mesh comparisons and iteration-limit trials are preserved.')
 para(d,'The digital record now separates numerical verification from physical validation. We can use the assembly as a bench prototype proposal, while collecting actual material curves and joint measurements for calibration. Exact Sony fit, real sound reduction, music leakage, heat, durability and sensory acceptance still need the measurements and sample tests listed in both reports.')
